    "url": "https://rivestack.io/blog/postgresql-jsonb-guide",
    "title": "PostgreSQL JSONB: A Complete Guide to Storing and Querying...",
    "snippet": "Apr 12, 2026         json stores the raw text exactly as you inserted it. Whitespace, key order, duplicate keys, all preserved.It strips whitespace, deduplicates keys (keeping the last value), and sorts object keys. Insertion is slightly slower because of the conversion, but reads are significantly faster because the database doesn't reparse anything. More importantly, JSONB supports GIN indexes, which make containment and existence queries fast even on large tables.   Summarize",
    "published": null
