    "title": "PostgreSQL JSON and JSONB: Query, Index, and Update JSON Columns",
    "snippet": "PostgreSQL does not support in-place mutation of individual JSON keys the way document databases do. Instead, you use the jsonb_set () function to produce a modified copy of the JSONB value and assign it back to the column in a standard UPDATE statement.",
